WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome back
to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.934
We're about to play a game
called "What's Behind Me?"

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:07.033
My partner tonight
is an incredible actress

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:10.234
and has a new children's book
out now, called "Busy Betty."

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:13.467
Give it up for the one and only
Reese Witherspoon!

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:18.334
Yeah, come on!

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:20.400
Welcome back, Reese!
-Thank you!

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.868
I'm so excited to be here!
-We love you.

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:23.267
Now, here's how the game works.

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:25.868
Reese and I will take turns
facing our backs to the curtain.

00:00:25.868 --> 00:00:27.067
Behind the curtain
will be something

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:28.634
neither of us have seen before.

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:30.734
Could be people, objects,
anything.

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:32.801
Once the curtain opens
and you pick up your card,

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:35.367
you have 45 seconds
to try to get the other person

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:36.968
to guess what's behind them.

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:39.067
You can say anything you want
or use gestures.

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:41.501
You just can't say any
of the words on your card.

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:43.734
Enough instructions?
-That's a lot of rules.

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:46.067
-All right, Reese,
you will be guessing first.

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:48.234
Let's get into position.
-Let's just see how this goes.

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:49.534
-Let's just see how this go--
oh.

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:50.601
-Wait.
-Look at this.

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:51.667
High budget.
-Ooh!

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:56.400
-This is --
This cost us $2 million.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.400
Aaron Judge's home-run ball
paid for this.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:02.667
-So, I'm gonna guess.
-You're gonna guess.

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:04.334
-I think, right?
So, you're gonna --

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:06.334
You're gonna watch it.
-Reese -- all right,

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:08.767
let's open the curtain
and see what's behind you.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:11.334
-Okay.

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:15.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.801
Okay.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:19.801 --> 00:01:22.701
Okay, okay.
Uh...okay.

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:25.200
It's the first president
of the United States.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.334
-George Washington.
-Yes.

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:29.467
And -- And, uh --
Uh, and, and, and, uh...

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:33.200
He's, uh --
There's a -- there's a baby --

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.601
there's a baby,
and the baby sits in...

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:38.767
-A stroller.
-When you're -- when you're --

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:40.501
when you're eating.
-In a high chair.

00:01:40.501 --> 00:01:44.767
-Yep. And the baby
is a famous horror movie.

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:48.300
-Predator.
-For Halloween, Halloween.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.567
-Oh, Jason!
The guy with the mask.

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:51.267
-The other "Halloween."
-"Scream" movie. Aah!

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:53.734
-No, the other "Halloween"!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:55.567
-He's a pumpkin!
He's a pumpkin!

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:56.701
-No, he's not a pumpkin.

00:01:56.701 --> 00:01:58.868
Actually, in the movie
"Halloween."

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:01.734
-Jamie Lee Curtis!
-Yes, close.

00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:03.901
But he's the person trying
to kill Jamie Lee Curtis.

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:06.067
-Jason! Jason!
-No, it's not Jason!

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:07.934
-Oh, oh!
Michael Myers! Michael Myers!

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:09.400
-Yes! That's correct.
[ Bell dings ]

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.934
George Washington feeding
Michael Myers in a high chair.

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:14.701
Can we see what it is?

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.334
-Oh!
-Well, hold on, sorry.

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:17.901
There you go.
-[ Screams ]

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:19.734
-He won't do it.
He doesn't want to eat it.

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:21.400
He doesn't want
to eat it at all.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.734
[ Laughter ]
-That's so weird.

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:24.801
-Thank you very much.
Thank you for trying, George.

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:26.767
You did a great job trying.
-Yeah, that was just weird.

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:27.968
-He does not want to eat.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:31.334
-Yay!

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:33.167
-That was a good actor.
-Who's Jason?

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:35.300
-Jason's "Friday the 13th."
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.634
Wait.
That's not Freddy Krueger?

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:38.334
-That's
"Nightmare on Elm Street."

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:39.601
-Oh, thank you.
-I don't even know that many

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:40.968
horror movies.
-Okay.

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:42.434
-Now it's my turn to guess.

00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:44.567
Here we go with
the million-dollar rotation.

00:02:44.567 --> 00:02:46.801
Here we go.
Wow.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:50.834
♪♪

00:02:50.834 --> 00:02:53.801
♪ Unh, unh, oww ♪
-♪ Raow ♪

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:55.133
-All right.
Now, all right.

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.501
Grab the blue card, look at it,

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:58.834
and now we have
to open the curtain.

00:02:58.834 --> 00:03:01.834
And then time starts
once you see what's behind me.

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:03.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:09.200
-[ Laughing ]

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:13.601
[ Laughter continues ]

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:14.801
-Okay!

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:17.334
This guy --
-I love your laugh.

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:18.467
That is so good.

00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:19.968
-He's one of the greatest
songwriters, okay?

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:21.968
-Oh, uh -- Paul McCartney.
-And he's been around

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:24.901
for a really long time,
and he loves to wear, like,

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:26.501
feathers and he --
-Elton John.

00:03:26.501 --> 00:03:27.534
-Yes!
[ Bell dings ]

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:30.467
Okay.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:34.234
He is doing something
that people used to do at --

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:37.767
I never, but --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:40.100
They never did this.
But you might have done this

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:43.901
as a kid at a Halloween party
in the '60s?

00:03:43.901 --> 00:03:45.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:47.334
The '80s?
Okay.

00:03:47.334 --> 00:03:49.067
-Uh, trick-or-treating.
-No kid does this.

00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:50.400
-No kid does this ever, no.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.133
-No, but it's -- it has fruit.
-Oh, bobbing for apples?

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:54.400
-Yes!
[ Bell dings ]

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:56.067 --> 00:03:57.701
That was good.
Okay, and then --

00:03:57.701 --> 00:03:58.934
-Yeah, you're right,
no one does this, yeah.

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:02.534
-He's at America's
almost favorite breakfast place.

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:04.033
The --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:07.033
There's so many things
on the menu at this place, like,

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:09.267
you don't even know
what to choose, because --

00:04:09.267 --> 00:04:11.334
-Waffle House?
-No, but thank you.

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:12.834
That is -- Yes, that's my
favorite breakfast place.

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:14.834
-Smothered and covered,
yeah, yeah.

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:17.367
-The next-best breakfast place.

00:04:17.367 --> 00:04:18.934
-Denny's?
-Yes!

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:22.734
-What? Elton John
bobbing for apples at a Denny's?

00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:25.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.734
Oh, he's being very picky.
[ Laughs ]

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:30.300
He's being very picky to see
which exact apple he wants.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.434
Oh, that's not how you do it.
-No hands. No hands.

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:33.868
-No hands, Elton.
-No hands.

00:04:33.868 --> 00:04:35.767
-Okay.
-People do not do that.

00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:37.133
-Thank you very much, Elton.
-People do not do that.

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:38.534
-He's being very picky
and selective.

00:04:38.534 --> 00:04:41.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Good job.

00:04:41.501 --> 00:04:44.067
-Okay, very nice here.

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:46.033
Reese, it is your turn to guess.

00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:47.167
Let's rotate.

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.834
♪♪

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:52.100
♪ Hey, I like to rotate ♪

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:54.000
♪ Yeah, cha, nah, la la ♪

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.267
Yeah, I love it.
All right.

00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:56.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:57.868
Let's see --

00:04:57.868 --> 00:04:59.701
It's a new reggae song called
"Let's Rotate."

00:04:59.701 --> 00:05:00.901
I don't know what that means.

00:05:00.901 --> 00:05:02.901
All right,
let's see what's behind you.

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:05.067
Open the curtain, please.

00:05:05.067 --> 00:05:13.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.868
That's very funny.

00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:17.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:18.868
Okay, it is --

00:05:18.868 --> 00:05:20.767
[ As Yoda ]
He talks like this.

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:23.467
-Oscar the Grouch?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:25.133
-He says in --
-Yoda!

00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:27.200
-[ Normal voice ] Yes, yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.601
He's an action --
action figure --

00:05:29.601 --> 00:05:31.901
it's an action figure
from the '80s.

00:05:31.901 --> 00:05:32.968
-He-Man.
-Yes!

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:35.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:37.067
All right.
They're doing something

00:05:37.067 --> 00:05:39.667
very famous that's on TikTok.

00:05:39.667 --> 00:05:41.734
-The squirrel dance.
Flossing.

00:05:41.734 --> 00:05:43.100
-Uh, it involves...
-The Gritty.

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:45.567
-...hitting each other with...
-Oh, punching.

00:05:45.567 --> 00:05:46.734
-No, but --
-Javelin.

00:05:46.734 --> 00:05:50.100
-No, it's a -- it's a burrito --
-Throw a burrito?

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.701
-No. But a burrito --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.701 --> 00:05:53.567
A burrito -- a burrito
is wrapped around --

00:05:53.567 --> 00:05:55.067
-Chipotle.
-No, yes.

00:05:55.067 --> 00:05:58.367
But -- but in a burrito,
the base of the burrito --

00:05:58.367 --> 00:05:59.734
-Taco.
-No, but a burrito --

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:01.634
-Tortilla. Tortilla!
-Yes!

00:06:01.634 --> 00:06:03.400
And they're using
the tortilla --

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:04.767
it's a big thing --
-Slap them with a tortilla.

00:06:04.767 --> 00:06:06.667
-Yes! Exactly!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:09.367
♪♪

00:06:09.367 --> 00:06:11.200
Wait, you gotta --

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.067
Reese, you have to see this.

00:06:14.067 --> 00:06:17.467
-[ Laughing ]

00:06:17.467 --> 00:06:18.834
It -- okay, this is just --
oh!

00:06:18.834 --> 00:06:20.234
-Oh, hey, whoa, He-Man!

00:06:20.234 --> 00:06:22.267
All right, it's the final round.

00:06:22.267 --> 00:06:24.501
-Okay.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:24.501 --> 00:06:25.901
What are we doing?

00:06:25.901 --> 00:06:28.567
-It's so silly.
I don't even understand.

00:06:28.567 --> 00:06:30.133
All right, it's the final round.

00:06:30.133 --> 00:06:31.868
Let's rotate.
-Okay.

00:06:31.868 --> 00:06:33.033
-All right, it's the last --
We got this.

00:06:33.033 --> 00:06:34.434
For all the --

00:06:34.434 --> 00:06:38.000
♪♪

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.267
All right.

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:43.734
Now, it is time
to see what is behind me.

00:06:43.734 --> 00:06:45.667
-What is behind him?
Okay.

00:06:45.667 --> 00:06:47.167
-Yes, here we go.
-Oh.

00:06:47.167 --> 00:06:49.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.901 --> 00:06:51.133
Wow!

00:06:51.133 --> 00:06:52.334
[ Laughter ]

00:06:52.334 --> 00:06:56.200
W-o-o-o-ow!

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:57.400
-Really?

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.567
[ Laughter ]
-Yes.

00:06:59.567 --> 00:07:01.801
Now, and I'm gonna hurry,
because this is gonna --

00:07:01.801 --> 00:07:03.534
this might not last very long.
-Okay, all right.

00:07:03.534 --> 00:07:04.934
-So I'm gonna hurry.
Okay, okay.

00:07:04.934 --> 00:07:06.901
So, this --
you would find these in Egypt.

00:07:06.901 --> 00:07:08.634
-A pyramid.
-Yes!

00:07:08.634 --> 00:07:10.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:10.367 --> 00:07:12.000
Uh...

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.734
Just the greatest movie ever.

00:07:13.734 --> 00:07:18.033
Tim Burton, and -- and you say
his name three times.

00:07:18.033 --> 00:07:19.133
-Beetlejuice!
-Yes!

00:07:19.133 --> 00:07:20.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:20.868 --> 00:07:22.968
Okay, and --
Beetlejuice is at the pyramid.

00:07:22.968 --> 00:07:26.267
-Yeah, but they're in
a very famous place.

00:07:26.267 --> 00:07:28.767
It's the city
of romance and love.

00:07:28.767 --> 00:07:30.367
-France!
-Yes, France!

00:07:30.367 --> 00:07:31.801
[ Bell dings ]
-At the Eiffel Tower?

00:07:31.801 --> 00:07:34.400
-Yes!
Okay, so, yes, it is...

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:35.434 --> 00:07:39.501
...a pyramid of Beetlejuices
in Paris.

00:07:39.501 --> 00:07:40.501
-What?

00:07:40.501 --> 00:07:42.167
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.167 --> 00:07:44.300
-Oh!
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:46.968
Oh, I -- see, now I get it.
-Yeah.

00:07:46.968 --> 00:07:48.367
-All right, we both
got credit for that one.

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:50.567
Reese Witherspoon, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:50.567 --> 00:07:52.868
Well done, dude.
It was very good.

00:07:52.868 --> 00:07:54.801
We're talking to Reese
after the break!

00:07:54.801 --> 00:07:56.300
Stick around, everybody!

